\[j_{\rm T}^{c} =C_{j_{\rm T}}\cdot j_{\rm T}^{unc} \tag{4.2}\] \[w^{c} =C_{w}\cdot w^{unc} \tag{4.3}\]

where \(j_{\rm T}^{c}\) and \(w^{c}\) are corrected \(j_{\rm T}\) and corrected weight of the \(j_{\rm T}\) in the histogram, \(j_{\rm T}^{unc}\) and \(w^{unc}\) are uncorrected values, \(C_{j_{\rm T}}\) and \(C_{w}\) are constant correction coefficients.

These coefficients actually change width (\(C_{j_{\rm T}}\)) and height (\(C_{w}\)) of the histogram. First step is to make exponential fits2 of both PYTHIA ("PYMC") and PYTHIA+GEANT+dAu

